## Extending the Compiler

### Setting Up Development

```sh
# Clone the compiler repository
git clone https://github.com/xiom-lang/xiom.git
cd xiom

# Build the compiler
xiom build

# Run the test suite
xiom test

# Make a change and test
xiom build && xiom test
```

### Adding a Compiler Pass

```xiom
// src/compiler/passes/my_pass.xi
use xiom_compiler::{Ast, CompilerContext, Pass};

pub type MyOptimization = {};

impl Pass for MyOptimization {
  fn name(self: &MyOptimization) -> Str {
    return "my-optimization";
  }

  fn run(self: &MyOptimization, ast: &mut Ast, ctx: &mut CompilerContext) {
    // Walk the AST and apply your transformation
    for func in ast.functions() {
      self.optimize_function(func);
    }
  }
}

fn optimize_function(self: &MyOptimization, func: &mut Function) {
  // Example: Replace x * 1 with x
  for stmt in func.body.stmts() {
    match stmt {
      BinaryOp(Mul, _, IntLiteral(1)) => {
        self.replace_with_left_operand(stmt);
      },
      _ => {},
    }
  }
}
```

### Registering a Pass

```xiom
// Register in the compiler driver
compiler.add_pass(MyOptimization{});
```

### Building Custom Tooling

```xiom
// Example: custom linter rule
use xiom_compiler;

fn main() -> Int {
  let compiler = xiom_compiler::Session::new();
  let ast = compiler.parse_file("src/main.xi").unwrap();

  // Walk all function calls
  for node in ast.walk() {
    match node {
      CallExpr{ func: Identifier("panic"), .. } => {
        io.println("Found panic!() call at " + node.location.to_str());
      },
      _ => {},
    }
  }
  return 0;
}
```

### Compiler Plugin System

```xiom
// Plugins are compiled separately and loaded at runtime
#[plugin]
fn my_lint_rule(node: &AstNode) -> Vec[Diagnostic] {
  var diagnostics = Vec[Diagnostic]();
  // Run custom analysis
  return diagnostics;
}
```

```sh
# Use a plugin:
xiom build --plugin my_lint.so src/
```

